From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m5agent <m5agent@m5stack.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 03:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] esp32: allow TIMG watchdog feeds to postpone later stages

The TIMG watchdog used timer_mod_anticipate_ns() for every arm operation.
That API intentionally preserves an earlier pending deadline.  A WDTFEED
that restarts stage 0 can therefore leave an already armed stage 1 deadline
in place, producing a system reset even though the guest fed the watchdog.

Use timer_mod_ns() for the watchdog stage timer.  This preserves the
existing timeout and interrupt behavior while allowing a feed to replace
the pending stage deadline with the newly armed one.
---
diff --git a/hw/timer/esp32_timg.c b/hw/timer/esp32_timg.c
--- a/hw/timer/esp32_timg.c
+++ b/hw/timer/esp32_timg.c
@@ -718,7 +718,12 @@ static void esp32_timg_wdt_arm(Esp32TimgWdtState *ws, uint64_t ns_now)
     }
     TIMG_DEBUG_LOG("%s: TG%d ns=0x%08llx stage %d count=0x%08x count_to_timeout=0x%08x ns_to_timeout=0x%08llx\n",
                    __func__, ws->parent->id, ns_now, ws->cur_stage, cur_count, count_to_timeout, ns_to_timeout);
-    timer_mod_anticipate_ns(&ws->stage_timer, ns_now + ns_to_timeout);
+    /*
+     * A watchdog feed must be able to postpone an already armed later stage.
+     * timer_mod_anticipate_ns() deliberately keeps the earlier deadline, which
+     * makes a stage-1 reset fire even after a successful WDTFEED.
+     */
+    timer_mod_ns(&ws->stage_timer, ns_now + ns_to_timeout);
 }
 
 static void esp32_timg_wdt_cb(void *opaque)
